{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791624733,"nonce":"J1ceK8AufAICaVvaRqyvRyMmHjg=","message":"Done. Released in ashui 0.1.2, with the final cleanup since.\n\n- Phase 3: 881ef19. Stylesheet.parse and Css.load parse natively; keyframes, :root variables, declarations, diagnostics and imports come from the native engine.\n- Phase 4: 881ef19 and 04aabbd. CompiledCss and -D ashui_css compile through blinc-css at build time, imports included, and embed the compiled sheet. Release packages bundle blinc-css per platform through native/hdlls.json and NativeInstall; a checkout builds it once with cargo install from the pinned blinc_abi. 7b2a39f makes the bundled tool executable, since haxelib drops file modes.\n- a15df4e: the Haxe CssParser, Selector and Media are removed, with tests/CssParse.hx, whose coverage is blinc_abi's parser tests and the parity runs. Query checks a selector at compile time with blinc-css --selector (blinc_abi 6e772f3).\n- The zero-length transitions in FormMotion: the native engine learns a state when its watch reacts, a round after the Haxe engine read it live, so one frame could apply an intermediate state. 13b4e55 records a move retargeted the instant it began as one move. FormMotion's tracks now match the Haxe engine's exactly.\n- Phase 5: native is faster than the Haxe engine (phase 2 table). The last runs were on a machine with a load average of 30-60; run alternately against the phase-2 build, they were no slower.","files":null}]}